Your rules for this feature, as the builders will follow them (each one applies to every case like it, not just the example):
  1. Whenever a customer returns an item, or asks for a refund because they changed their mind, refund the amount actually paid for the goods after any coupon. Refund all of it if the return is within 14 days of delivery, half of it if it is after day 14 and up to day 30, and nothing at all after day 30 (the request is refused).
  2. Whenever a refund is calculated, the shipping fee is not refunded unless the goods are damaged. A wrong size does not count as damaged. When the goods are damaged, the shipping fee is refunded.
  3. Whenever a customer asks for a refund on a whole order, calculate it with the same standard refund rules as any other refund (by days since delivery, with shipping excluded unless the goods are damaged). Then subtract any amount already refunded on that order. The total refunded across all requests on the order can never exceed the amount the customer paid.
  4. Whenever an order is cancelled or returned before it has shipped, refund it to the original payment method, charge no ₹50 fee, and do not refund the shipping fee.
  5. Whenever a refund is paid out, send it back by the same method the customer paid with (card payments to the card, store credit as store credit).
  6. Whenever any amount is calculated, including a refund after the coupon and shipping are applied, round it down to the nearest whole rupee and discard the paise.
  7. Whenever a cart's loyalty points are calculated, the order earns points only if its item total after the discount (goods price minus discount, excluding shipping and tax) is at least ₹500 and it was not paid with store credit. It then earns 1 point for every full ₹100 of that post-discount item total. Shipping earns nothing and there is no tax rule. An order under ₹500 or paid with store credit earns 0 points. Only final-sale orders earn double points, and regular customers do not.
  8. Whenever a refund is given on an order, the customer keeps the loyalty points already earned on that order, because there is no rule for taking points back after a refund.
  9. Whenever the sales or daily summary is shown, "Orders" is the count of every order in the list or for the day, including store-credit orders. It shows 0 only when there are no orders at all.
  10. Whenever the sales or daily summary is shown, "Revenue" is the sum, over card orders only, of each order's items after discount plus its shipping. When there are no card orders, Revenue is ₹0 and average order value is ₹0 (the average is defined as 0 when there are no card orders), and no error is shown.
  11. When a customer reports a damaged item more than 14 days after delivery, how much of the item price is refunded? -> A) The full item amount, as long as the damage is reported within 90 days of delivery.
